00:06:09.600 --> 00:06:17.810
Runaway Duck by David Lyon, read by Orson Bean.

00:06:18.520 --> 00:06:29.550
One morning, Sebastian Willowfrost was playing in the garage.

00:06:30.800 --> 00:06:35.450
He was rolling Egbert, his favorite toy, around on the floor.

00:06:37.180 --> 00:06:44.000
Egbert was a carved wooden duck with wheels and a long nylon string for pulling.

00:06:45.130 --> 00:06:49.310
One wheel had a plaque on which Sebastian had written his name.

00:06:50.960 --> 00:06:54.310
Suddenly, Sebastian's father called him in for lunch.

00:06:55.140 --> 00:06:59.940
Just a minute, Sebastian tied Egbert to the bumper of his father's car.

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:01.700
so that he couldn't roll away.

00:07:08.000 --> 00:07:09.740
Sebastian's father ate quickly.

00:07:10.710 --> 00:07:13.110
He was going on a long business trip.

00:07:14.690 --> 00:07:19.950
Sebastian forgot that Egbert was tied to the bumper of his father's car.

00:07:22.560 --> 00:07:29.550
By the time Sebastian remembered, Egbert was doing 60 miles an hour down Route 95.

00:07:33.000 --> 00:07:35.580
Racing around a sharp mountain turn,

00:07:36.180 --> 00:07:37.720
Egbert's tie string broke.

00:07:39.000 --> 00:07:42.840
Egbert sailed off into empty space.

00:07:46.610 --> 00:07:49.630
For ten seconds, Egbert flew like a real duck.

00:07:50.560 --> 00:07:54.990
But then he fell down, down, down

00:07:54.990 --> 00:07:57.080
into Emerald Valley.

00:07:58.780 --> 00:07:59.980
Luckily, Egbert...

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:04.850
fell into a stream where he was carried forward by the force of the water.

00:08:05.700 --> 00:08:08.060
Egbert rolled and floated on,

00:08:08.640 --> 00:08:15.280
past Bottleburg, Carburg, and Burgerburg, out into the sea.

00:08:18.740 --> 00:08:24.100
Meanwhile, Sebastian prayed that Egbert was safe and that he might return.

00:08:25.070 --> 00:08:29.970
He wrote several poems in memory of Egbert and tried to forget the...

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:38.810
whole tragedy by playing baseball. One night in early September, Egbert was attacked by a shark.

00:08:39.620 --> 00:08:46.990
The shark pulled Egbert down into the ocean. He bit off one of Egbert's wheels, discovered that it

00:08:46.990 --> 00:08:59.980
was wood, and swam away in disgust. Egbert floated up past a clownfish, a sea turtle, and a pufffish.

00:09:00.990 --> 00:09:02.610
The wheel floated up alone.

00:09:06.750 --> 00:09:12.330
After some time, a wave tossed Egbert onto an almost deserted isle.

00:09:13.600 --> 00:09:15.370
Voila! Un canard!

00:09:15.800 --> 00:09:16.720
Whoopee! A duck!

00:09:17.240 --> 00:09:22.340
Cried Jacques Divin, poet, shipwreck survivor, and Frenchman.

00:09:25.650 --> 00:09:29.980
Jacques wrote a long poem about Egbert called Song...

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:41.530
to a duck oh what luck to find a duck upon a desert isle he's missing a wheel and paints

00:09:41.530 --> 00:09:53.750
all peeled but nevertheless he smiles the next day sailors on a french merchant vessel

00:09:53.750 --> 00:09:59.900
spotted Jacques and carried him and Egbert to France there was

00:10:00.120 --> 00:10:02.060
Much excitement over the castaways.

00:10:02.830 --> 00:10:05.730
The president of France met the ship at port.

00:10:09.180 --> 00:10:12.190
Le Monde, an important French newspaper,

00:10:12.660 --> 00:10:16.260
published a photo of Egbert and a copy of Jacques's poem.

00:10:17.280 --> 00:10:21.700
Sebastian happened to see Egbert's picture at a local newsstand.

00:10:22.490 --> 00:10:27.420
He immediately went home and wrote a letter to the president of France.

00:10:28.270 --> 00:10:29.970
Please, he wrote...

00:10:30.020 --> 00:10:40.780
Edward Holmes. Jacques was enjoying dinner when the French president showed him the letter. Jacques

00:10:40.780 --> 00:10:50.260
tossed his napkin on the table and stood up. But this is my duck, Jacques cried. Why, they are not

00:10:50.260 --> 00:10:58.960
the same. They cannot be. Jacques went for a long walk.

00:11:01.080 --> 00:11:07.510
Meanwhile, the president's daughter checked to see whether Sebastian's name was on Egbert's right front wheel.

00:11:08.840 --> 00:11:14.990
Unfortunately, this wheel was now in Portugal, where a little girl was wearing it on a necklace.

00:11:15.410 --> 00:11:21.270
When he got back to the palace, Jacques announced,

00:11:21.710 --> 00:11:25.550
I will return the duck this evening by air post.

00:11:26.310 --> 00:11:29.390
The president's daughter kissed Jacques on the cheek.

00:11:33.930 --> 00:11:38.230
Sebastian received the package and a letter two weeks later.

00:11:38.550 --> 00:11:43.530
Everything seemed perfect.

00:11:44.780 --> 00:11:50.580
Sometimes, though, Sebastian tried to imagine what had happened to Egbert's front wheel.

00:11:51.100 --> 00:11:59.980
And sometimes, far, far away, a little girl in Portugal wondered just who Sebastian was.

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:02.260
Sebastian Willowfrost was.

