One day, Ping was fishing upside down

00:24:38.300 --> 00:24:39.660
with his head in the water.

00:24:39.800 --> 00:24:42.750
He didn't hear his master calling,

00:24:42.910 --> 00:24:44.390
La la la.

00:24:45.000 --> 00:24:47.060
to come back to the boat.

00:24:47.620 --> 00:24:49.440
Ping is left behind.

00:24:50.870 --> 00:24:54.250
Ping had lots of adventures while he was lost,

00:24:54.410 --> 00:24:59.230
but finally he found his family and his home.

00:25:01.050 --> 00:25:01.550
Once.

00:25:02.010 --> 00:25:07.490
I got lost and just like paying, I was really glad to see my family again.

00:25:08.250 --> 00:25:11.750
This book is so wonderful, I want you to read it too.

00:25:12.150 --> 00:25:14.850
So go and find it at your public library.

00:25:18.450 --> 00:25:19.070
Well...

00:25:19.160 --> 00:25:23.640
I'm sure these ducks and geese will have a great winter vacation here on the Chesapeake.

00:25:24.120 --> 00:25:25.400
And when spring rolls around,

00:25:25.690 --> 00:25:27.670
They'll head back up north where they came from.

00:25:28.410 --> 00:25:29.970
And if you've ever been away from home,

00:25:30.000 --> 00:25:40.860
You know just how good it feels to get back because as the old saying goes there's no place like home. Just ask Egbert

00:25:42.650 --> 00:25:44.070
I'll see you next time

